Hello guys! How are you doing?

Please, leave the candy you were about to eat on the table and let’s ready today’s update (c’mon, you’ll get a lot more during Halloween). Update 0.9 is mostly focused on polishing the game, but there are also new things on the gameplay itself, such as different difficulty for each level.

Here is a summary of what has changed. You can read more details below it:
[list]
[*]Changed the sound effects of the game;
[*]Sound effects are now 3D (you can hear where they are playing from);
[*]Changed the songs of the levels (background music);
[*]Improved muzzle flash, shot and hit particles of the weapons;
[*]Improved screen shake;
[*]Improved the Store’s visual;
[*]Performance optimization;
[*]New water visual;
[*]Improved the pace of the game (more frenetic);
[*]Now each map has its own difficulty (easiest to hardest);
[*]Balanced damage of swords;
[*]Liz can now charge the sword special attack while running;
[*]Liz can now throw daggers while running (what a ninja);
[*]Fixed Liz’ movement bug after getting revived;
[*]Changed prices of new maps and characters.
[/list]

Check the new stuff by watching this uncomment gameplay (I know you skipped all the text above):
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ox0sSpzsDnY


Now, the details…

[h1]New sounds[/h1]
You can finally hear different fire guns sounds when you shoot, not just the same one for pistol, submachine gun, shotgun and so on (I can still hear that old sound in my dreams…). That’s right, a lot of new sound effects were added to the game and they are now 3D, meaning you can hear the direction they are coming from.
The background music’s were also changed, excepted for the Main Menu and Map 03, which remain the same. Let me know if you enjoyed the new ones.

[h1]New particles and visuals[/h1]
Guns and other weapons now shoot cool particles! RIP old lame green line (if you got that, thanks! That means you’ve been following the project for a long time).  Other particles were improved as well, such as explosions.
The enemies now shake a little bit when you hit them and their dialog is surrounded by a dialog box. Screen shake was also improved. The water looks more beautiful too.

[img]https://media.giphy.com/media/cCbijUlAm6w4cx4JTj/giphy.gif[/img]

[h1]New store[/h1]
The rune displays were rearranged and improved so you can easily understand their effects and who can use them.

[b]Old[/b]
[img]https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/steamcommunity/public/images/clans/32265385/ca8b434d9c2da556be6bd47af2cb7c9b3e233904.png[/img]

[b]New[/b]
[img]https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/steamcommunity/public/images/clans/32265385/e1707a824a4e2b88370cbdf67c06a59350c86557.png[/img]

[h1]New difficulty[/h1]
Each map has now its own difficulty. That means you won’t necessarily reach a certain round as easy as you reached in the previous map. Pigeons are faster, do more damage and have even less mercy, but I now you won’t let them win without putting up a good fight.
You will also notice that the pace has changed. Pigeons will now spawn closer to you. This also fix a problem while playing on a big map on the previous versions, in which you had to wait a lot for some pigeons to come to you, specially if you had unlocked a lot of paths. 

[h1]What comes next? [/h1]
Pigeons Attack is close to the final version. We will now work on Steam achievements, some basic tutorials for new players and continue polishing and optimizing the game. But don’t worry, we will keep the game updated with new stuff even after the 1.0 version, so don’t forget to give us your feedback about things that should be improved or that you would like to see in the game.


Thank you for reading today’s update and for playing Pigeons Attack! See you in the next one.

Hello guys! How are you doing?

If you are reading this, pigeons haven’t gotten you yet (glad to know that). Today’s updates focus basically on fixing some bugs. 

Here are the fixes and some minor improvements:
[list]
[*](Coop) Fixed bug where reviving partner and dying at the same time could cause the match to finish, but you partner could still fight;
[*](Coop) Fixed bug where player 2 could press start to join the game even if the player 1 were dead (maybe they just wanted revenge you);
[*](Coop) Fixed bug where Ron’s magic was hitting the partner revive trigger, not allowing to hit the incoming pigeons;
[*]Fixed Purple Staff’s spheres position;
[*]Adjusted map four terrain so Ron’s magic doesn’t hit the floor too often when aiming forward;
[*]Fixed bug where Ron’s magic could collide with himself;
[*]Fixed visual bug when two players use the special attack (F);
[*]Fixed bug where camp fire could block a pigeon movement (now it also hurts you)
[*]Fixed bug where some objects were blocking pigeons path on map four.
[*]Fixed bug where right stick wasn’t maintaining the aim/player rotation when using a joystick;
[*]Added aim indication when using a joystick;
[*]You can now close the pause menu by pressing “B” when using a joystick.
[/list]

Please, let us know about any other bug.

We will now work hard on the next big update. Thanks for playing Pigeons Attack!
